IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 12, Division 2 (ss 205 to 212): prohibited conduct on financial benchmarks. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Reading an answer, the markers and the party of a regulative rule are explained at the head of sfab-division-1.l4 and in NOTES.md.
-- ss 211 and 212 are shown "[Repealed by Act 4 of 2017]" and are rows of the coverage table, not rules.

DECLARE `s 207 to s 209 prohibited act` IS ONE OF
    `s 207(1) do a thing, cause a thing to be done or engage in a course of conduct for the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance as to a financial benchmark`
    `s 207(2) do a thing that creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance as to a financial benchmark, knowingly or recklessly`
    `s 209 make a statement, disseminate information or express an opinion that is false or misleading in a material particular to a person administering a financial benchmark`

§ `s 205: application of Division 2`

-- src:34745 | 205. This Division applies to —
@ref s 205 (src:34745-34745)
GIVEN
    `this Division applies to the act occurring within Singapore (the answer under section 205(a))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 205(a) answer for this act? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `this Division applies to the act occurring outside Singapore (the answer under section 205(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 205(b) answer for this act? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205 this Division applies to the act` MEANS
    IF (`this Division applies to the act occurring within Singapore (the answer under section 205(a))` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`this Division applies to the act occurring outside Singapore (the answer under section 205(b))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Division applies to"

-- src:34747 | (a) acts occurring within Singapore in relation to financial
-- src:34748 | benchmarks, whether administered in Singapore or
-- src:34749 | elsewhere; and
@ref s 205(a) (src:34747-34749)
GIVEN
    `the act occurs within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act occur within Singapore?
    `the act relates to a financial benchmark, whether administered in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the act relates to a financial benchmark, whether administered in Singapore or elsewhere?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(a) this Division applies to the act occurring within Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the act occurs within Singapore` AND `the act relates to a financial benchmark, whether administered in Singapore or elsewhere`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "acts occurring within Singapore in relation to financial benchmarks" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [SCOPE]

-- src:34751 | (b) acts occurring outside Singapore in relation to financial
-- src:34752 | benchmarks that are administered in Singapore.
@ref s 205(b) (src:34751-34752)
GIVEN
    `the act occurs outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act occur outside Singapore?
    `the act relates to a financial benchmark that is administered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the act relates to a financial benchmark that is administered in Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(b) this Division applies to the act occurring outside Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the act occurs outside Singapore` AND `the act relates to a financial benchmark that is administered in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "acts occurring outside Singapore in relation to financial benchmarks that are administered in Singapore" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [SCOPE]

§ `s 206: interpretation of Division 2`

-- src:34761 | 206. In this Division —
-- src:34763 | “administer”, in relation to a financial benchmark, means the
-- src:34764 | activity of administering the financial benchmark;
@ref s 206 "administer" (src:34761-34764)
GIVEN
    `the act is administering a financial benchmark as section 2(1) defines it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 2(1) "administering a financial benchmark" answer for this activity? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206 "administer" the activity is to administer the financial benchmark` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act is administering a financial benchmark as section 2(1) defines it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the act is administering a financial benchmark as section 2(1) defines it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the activity of administering the financial benchmark"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer under section 2(1) "administering a financial benchmark" was not given

-- src:34766 | “international body” means the European Central Bank, the
-- src:34767 | Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries, and such
-- src:34768 | other international bodies as may be prescribed by
-- src:34769 | regulations made under section 341;
@ref s 206 "international body" (src:34766-34769)
GIVEN
    `the body is the European Central Bank` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the body is the European Central Bank?
    `the body is the Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the body is the Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries?
    `regulations under section 341 prescribe the body as an international body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations made under section 341 prescribe the body as an international body?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206 "international body" the body is an international body` MEANS
    IF `the body is the European Central Bank` OR `the body is the Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries` OR `regulations under section 341 prescribe the body as an international body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the European Central Bank, the Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries, and such other international bodies as may be prescribed"

-- src:34771 | “public authority” means —
-- src:34773 | (a) any ministry or department of the Government, or
-- src:34774 | any statutory body, or any board, commission,
-- src:34775 | committee or similar body, whether corporate or
-- src:34776 | unincorporated, established under a public Act for a
-- src:34777 | public purpose;
-- src:34779 | (b) in relation to a foreign country or territory, an
-- src:34780 | authority of the foreign country or territory, or any
-- src:34781 | board, commission, committee or similar body,
-- src:34782 | whether corporate or unincorporated, established
-- src:34783 | under the law of the foreign country or territory for
-- src:34784 | a public purpose; or
-- src:34786 | (c) such other organisation as the Authority may
-- src:34787 | prescribe by regulations made under section 341.
@ref s 206 "public authority" (src:34771-34787)
GIVEN
    `the body is a ministry or department of the Government, a statutory body, or a board, commission, committee or similar body established under a public Act for a public purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a ministry or department of the Government, or a statutory body, or a board, commission, committee or similar body, whether corporate or unincorporated, established under a public Act for a public purpose?
    `the body is an authority of a foreign country or territory, or a board, commission, committee or similar body established under its law for a public purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body, in relation to a foreign country or territory, an authority of that country or territory, or a board, commission, committee or similar body, whether corporate or unincorporated, established under its law for a public purpose?
    `the Authority has prescribed the organisation as a public authority by regulations under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed the organisation as a public authority by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206 "public authority" the body is a public authority` MEANS
    IF `the body is a ministry or department of the Government, a statutory body, or a board, commission, committee or similar body established under a public Act for a public purpose` OR `the body is an authority of a foreign country or territory, or a board, commission, committee or similar body established under its law for a public purpose` OR `the Authority has prescribed the organisation as a public authority by regulations under section 341`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“public authority” means"

§ `s 207: manipulation of financial benchmarks`

-- src:34793 | 207.—(1) A person must not do any thing, cause any thing to be
-- src:34794 | done or engage in any course of conduct, if the person’s purpose, or
-- src:34795 | any of the person’s purposes, for doing that thing, causing that thing
-- src:34796 | to be done or engaging in that course of conduct (as the case may be)
-- src:34797 | is to create a false or misleading appearance as to the price, value,
-- src:34798 | performance or rate of any financial benchmark.
@ref s 207(1) (src:34793-34798)
GIVEN
    `the person did a thing, caused a thing to be done or engaged in a course of conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person do a thing, cause a thing to be done or engage in a course of conduct?
    `the purpose or one of the purposes is to create a false or misleading appearance as to the price, value, performance or rate of a financial benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person's purpose, or one of the person's purposes, for it to create a false or misleading appearance as to the price, value, performance or rate of any financial benchmark?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1) the person's conduct contravenes the bar on conduct done to create a false appearance as to a financial benchmark` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person did a thing, caused a thing to be done or engaged in a course of conduct`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person must not do any thing, cause any thing to be done or engage in any course of conduct" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]
        IF `the purpose or one of the purposes is to create a false or misleading appearance as to the price, value, performance or rate of a financial benchmark`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person’s purpose, or any of the person’s purposes" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [IF]

@ref s 207(1) (src:34793-34798)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 207 to s 209 prohibited act`
`s 207(1) a person must not act for the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance as to a financial benchmark` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "a person"
    SHANT `s 207(1) do a thing, cause a thing to be done or engage in a course of conduct for the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance as to a financial benchmark`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person did a thing, caused it to be done or engaged in a course of conduct for the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance as to the price, value, performance or rate of a financial benchmark (section 207(1))"

-- src:34802 | (2) A person must not do any thing, cause any thing to be done or
-- src:34803 | engage in any course of conduct that creates, or is likely to create, a
-- src:34808 | false or misleading appearance, as to the price, value, performance or
-- src:34809 | rate of any financial benchmark, if —
-- src:34811 | (a) the person knows that doing that thing, causing that thing
-- src:34812 | to be done or engaging in that course of conduct (as the
-- src:34813 | case may be) will create, or will likely create, that false or
-- src:34814 | misleading appearance; or
-- src:34816 | (b) the person is reckless as to whether doing that thing,
-- src:34817 | causing that thing to be done or engaging in that course of
-- src:34818 | conduct (as the case may be) will create, or will likely
-- src:34819 | create, that false or misleading appearance.
@ref s 207(2) (src:34802-34819)
GIVEN
    `the person did a thing, caused a thing to be done or engaged in a course of conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person do a thing, cause a thing to be done or engage in a course of conduct?
    `the thing creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance as to the price, value, performance or rate of a financial benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the thing create, or is it likely to create, a false or misleading appearance as to the price, value, performance or rate of any financial benchmark?
    `the person knows that the thing will create, or will likely create, that false or misleading appearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person know that doing the thing will create, or will likely create, that false or misleading appearance?
    `the person is reckless as to whether the thing will create, or will likely create, that false or misleading appearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person reckless as to whether doing the thing will create, or will likely create, that false or misleading appearance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(2) the person's conduct contravenes the bar on conduct that creates a false appearance as to a financial benchmark knowingly or recklessly` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person did a thing, caused a thing to be done or engaged in a course of conduct` AND `the thing creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance as to the price, value, performance or rate of a financial benchmark`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]
        IF `the person knows that the thing will create, or will likely create, that false or misleading appearance` OR `the person is reckless as to whether the thing will create, or will likely create, that false or misleading appearance`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if" "the person knows that doing that thing" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [IF]

@ref s 207(2) (src:34802-34819)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 207 to s 209 prohibited act`
`s 207(2) a person must not do a thing that creates a false or misleading appearance as to a financial benchmark knowingly or recklessly` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "a person"
    SHANT `s 207(2) do a thing that creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance as to a financial benchmark, knowingly or recklessly`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person did a thing that creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance as to a financial benchmark, knowing or reckless that it would (section 207(2))"

§ `s 208: exception for conduct pursuant to policy requirement`

-- src:34825 | 208. Section 207 does not apply in respect of any thing done or to
-- src:34826 | be done or any course of conduct engaged by, or by a person acting on
-- src:34827 | behalf of, a public authority or international body, whether in
-- src:34828 | Singapore or elsewhere —
-- src:34830 | (a) in respect of monetary policy;
-- src:34832 | (b) in respect of policies with respect to exchange rates, the
-- src:34833 | management of public debt or foreign exchange reserves;
-- src:34834 | or
-- src:34836 | (c) for the purpose of managing the price or value of any
-- src:34837 | commodity.
@ref s 208 (src:34825-34837)
GIVEN
    `the thing was done by, or by a person acting on behalf of, a public authority (the answer under section 206)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing done, or the course of conduct engaged in, by or on behalf of a public authority? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the question under section 206 "public authority", or NOTHING if not known)
    `the thing was done by, or by a person acting on behalf of, an international body (the answer under section 206)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing done, or the course of conduct engaged in, by or on behalf of an international body? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the question under section 206 "international body", or NOTHING if not known)
    `the thing was done in respect of monetary policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the thing was done in respect of monetary policy?
    `the thing was done in respect of policies with respect to exchange rates, the management of public debt or foreign exchange reserves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the thing was done in respect of policies with respect to exchange rates, the management of public debt or foreign exchange reserves?
    `the thing was done for the purpose of managing the price or value of a commodity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the thing was done for the purpose of managing the price or value of a commodity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 208 section 207 does not apply to the thing done` MEANS
    IF ((`the thing was done by, or by a person acting on behalf of, a public authority (the answer under section 206)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the thing was done by, or by a person acting on behalf of, an international body (the answer under section 206)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND (`the thing was done in respect of monetary policy` OR `the thing was done in respect of policies with respect to exchange rates, the management of public debt or foreign exchange reserves` OR `the thing was done for the purpose of managing the price or value of a commodity`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 207 does not apply in respect of any thing done or to be done or any course of conduct engaged by, or by a person acting on behalf of, a public authority or international body"

§ `s 209: false or misleading statements to a benchmark administrator`

-- src:34843 | 209. A person must not make a statement, disseminate any
-- src:34844 | information or express any opinion that is false or misleading in a
-- src:34845 | material particular to a person who carries out the activity of
-- src:34846 | administering a financial benchmark if —
-- src:34848 | (a) the person intends that the statement, information or
-- src:34849 | opinion be used for the purpose of administering a
-- src:34850 | financial benchmark; and
-- src:34852 | (b) the person knows or ought reasonably to have known that
-- src:34853 | the statement, information or opinion is false or misleading
-- src:34858 | in a material particular, or is reckless as to whether the
-- src:34859 | statement, information or opinion is false or misleading in
-- src:34860 | a material particular.
@ref s 209 (src:34843-34860)
GIVEN
    `the person made a statement, disseminated information or expressed an opinion that is false or misleading in a material particular to a person who administers a financial benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person make a statement, disseminate information or express an opinion that is false or misleading in a material particular to a person who carries out the activity of administering a financial benchmark?
    `the person intends that the statement, information or opinion be used for the purpose of administering a financial benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person intend that the statement, information or opinion be used for the purpose of administering a financial benchmark?
    `the person knows or ought reasonably to have known that it is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person know, or ought the person reasonably to have known, that the statement, information or opinion is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person is reckless as to whether it is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person reckless as to whether the statement, information or opinion is false or misleading in a material particular?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209 the person's statement contravenes the bar on false or misleading statements to a benchmark administrator` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person made a statement, disseminated information or expressed an opinion that is false or misleading in a material particular to a person who administers a financial benchmark`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person who carries out the activity of administering a financial benchmark" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]
        IF `the person intends that the statement, information or opinion be used for the purpose of administering a financial benchmark` AND (`the person knows or ought reasonably to have known that it is false or misleading in a material particular` OR `the person is reckless as to whether it is false or misleading in a material particular`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if" "the person intends that the statement, information or opinion be used" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [IF]

@ref s 209 (src:34843-34860)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 207 to s 209 prohibited act`
`s 209 a person must not make a false or misleading statement to a person administering a financial benchmark` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "a person"
    SHANT `s 209 make a statement, disseminate information or express an opinion that is false or misleading in a material particular to a person administering a financial benchmark`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person made a statement, disseminated information or expressed an opinion that is false or misleading in a material particular to a person administering a financial benchmark, intending it to be used for that purpose (section 209)"

§ `s 210: penalties under Division 2`

-- src:34866 | 210.—(1) Any person who contravenes any of the provisions of this
-- src:34867 | Division shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:34868 | to a fine not exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:34869 | exceeding 7 years or to both.
@ref s 210(1) (src:34866-34869)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 210(1) the penalty on conviction for contravening a provision of Division 2` MEANS
    Penalty OF 250000, 84, TRUE, 0  -- fine not exceeding $250,000; imprisonment not exceeding 7 years (84 months); "or to both"; no daily fine stated

@ref s 210(1) (src:34866-34869)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes a provision of Division 2 (the answer under the section that is contravened)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under the section of Division 2 that the person is said to contravene answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes a provision of Division 2 (the answer under the section that is contravened)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes any of the provisions of this Division" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]

-- src:34873 | (2) No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an
-- src:34874 | offence in respect of a contravention of any of the provisions of this
-- src:34875 | Division after —
-- src:34877 | (a) a court has made an order against the person for the
-- src:34878 | payment of a civil penalty under section 232; or
-- src:34880 | (b) the person has entered into an agreement with the
-- src:34881 | Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a
-- src:34882 | civil penalty under section 232(5),
-- src:34884 | in respect of that contravention.
@ref s 210(2) (src:34873-34884)
GIVEN
    `a court has made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 232 in respect of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 232 in respect of the contravention?
    `the person has entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 232(5) in respect of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a civil penalty under section 232(5) in respect of the contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(2) proceedings for an offence in respect of the contravention are barred` MEANS
    IF `a court has made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 232 in respect of the contravention` OR `the person has entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 232(5) in respect of the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an offence in respect of a contravention of any of the provisions of this Division after" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
